The FM voice (crates/dsp/src/fm/) is written in Rust from the public Yamaha DX7
voice format and algorithm tables. Its envelope and level behaviour follows the
reference of "music-synthesizer-for-android" (msfa), Copyright Google Inc.,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://github.com/google/music-synthesizer-for-android). No code or data from
Dexed (GPL-3.0) is used.

The wavetables and attack samples of the table oscillator (PPG Wave and Roland D-50
models) are generated by the engine's own code at start-up. They are not taken
from any instrument's ROM.
